          "sourceRegion": "Question 9, right of introductory stem",
          "description": "Horizontal parallel lines AB and CD have matching right-pointing mid-line arrows. Transversal YQPX rises from lower left to upper right. P and Q sit below their intersections. An obtuse arc above AB between PA and PX is labelled a without a degree symbol.",
